          "seo_description": "Your back has been hurting for weeks, and you finally decide to ask your supervisor if you can use a stool at your station—standing for a full shift just is not going to work for a while. She says she will get back to you, but one week goes by, then another. You follow up. This time she tells you that standing is part of the job—and if you can not do it, you might need to find a new place to work.",
          "seo_keywords": "employee disability rights nc, ada accommodation north carolina, workplace disability discrimination, reasonable accommodation at work, nc employment law disability, americans with disabilities act nc, wrongful termination disability, interactive process ada, nc workplace rights, disability retaliation nc",
